    T0 (owner, 2026-11-19): the port's split selects exactly (7n+9)/10 distinct ids among the input's
    
    The split-ids file is used only when it names exactly (7n+9)/10 distinct ids, all among the
    input's; otherwise a draw seeded 42 of that many distinct ids from the input's (sorted, so row
    order cannot change it). The input check already stops any input with a missing or repeated id,
    so the draw is over the n present, distinct ids. Real data keeps SAS's split; parity 10/10 PASS.
    Tests: real data, files that do not fit, n = 4, 5, 10, seeded draw.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

